# <%= @name %>

A small Ruby CLI that prints its text arguments separated by spaces.

Requires Ruby 3.4 or newer. This initial implementation has no external service
dependencies.

## Usage

    <%= @name %> hello world
    <%= @name %> --help
    <%= @name %> --version
    <%= @name %> -- --text-starting-with-a-dash

Successful output goes to stdout. Invalid options and missing text go to stderr
with exit status 2. A closed output pipe exits cleanly.

## Install from source

    gem build <%= @name %>.gemspec
    gem install ./<%= @name %>-0.1.0.gem

This repository's creation does not publish the gem or reserve its name.
After a release has actually been published, RubyGems installation is available:

    gem install <%= @name %>

## Development

    bin/setup
    bundle exec rake check
    bundle exec rake audit

Commit Gemfile.lock after dependency installation. It pins development tools;
users installing the gem resolve the dependencies declared in its gemspec.
The versioned ruby-repo-kit development dependency supplies repository and release
operations. That gem version must be available from the configured source before
contributors or hosted CI can install the development bundle.

Local checks include Ruby linting, tests with coverage (90% lines, 80% branches),
repository checks and installation of the built package.
The separate audit task updates a vulnerability database and
needs network access. CI additionally checks pull-request commits and exercises
Ruby 3.4/4.0 on Linux and Ruby 4.0 on macOS. These are configured checks, not a
claim that a new repository has already passed them.

See [contributing](CONTRIBUTING.md), [architecture](ARCHITECTURE.md),
[security](SECURITY.md), [conduct](CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md), and
[release setup](docs/releasing.md).

